 "claim": "A removal opens exactly the cuts that point away from it. Assemble a knot space from pieces along a tree of splices, and orient every cut from its point side to its line side; every cut stays a simple 3-edge cut of the whole space. (1) Removing a line M holds every cut whose point side does not contain M (the cut points toward M) and opens every cut whose point side contains M (the cut points away from M). (2) At a held cut the three ports are tied, and the far point side keeps exactly the circuits of its own system: the knots of its contraction without its closing line, whatever M is. (3) At an opened cut the port patterns are exactly those the near contraction (which contains M) allows on the closing line once M is gone, so M reaches the far line side only through that interface. These follow from HUB-GLUE A-C applied to each cut. Checked on chains and trees of three and four pieces (K4^(3) and Fano pieces, 10 to 16 points): every removal, every cut.",
